2026-02-10 02:54:05,886 - DocumentGraderNode - INFO: Retrieved document What is an Underlying Asset

Underlying assets are the basic financial instruments or commodities that derivatives like options and futures are based on. The value of a derivative depends directly on the price or performance of its underlying asset, making these assets crucial in trading. Examples include stocks, bonds, commodities, or indexes. is relevant
